  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A break at the office</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"I work at a bank downtown. Right now I’m having lunch with a coworker. We’re sitting outside, and she’s telling me about her new apartment."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which sentence describes a routine, something generally true?</li>
      <li>Which actions are happening at this moment?</li>
      <li>What small verb comes before each <span class="ex">-ing</span> word?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Every sentence contains the subject-matched form of be and an unchanged verb-ing activity form.">
    <h3>Discovery check: choose the pattern</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the subject to choose <b>am</b>, <b>is</b>, or <b>are</b>. Two gaps need the <b>-ing</b> verb itself.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="am">am</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="working">working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="waiting">waiting</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The live elevator message says, “I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="am" data-hint="The subject I takes am before waiting." data-fix="I am waiting for the elevator." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> waiting for the elevator.”</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The office update states that Lena uses <span class="ex">she</span>. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="The subject she takes is before talking." data-fix="She is talking to a client." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> talking to a client.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The team has already arranged tonight's shift. They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-hint="The plural subject they takes are before working." data-fix="They are working late tonight." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> working late tonight.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The live weather camera shows rain. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-hint="The subject it takes is before raining." data-fix="It is raining outside." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> raining outside.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Marcos’s temporary schedule says he is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="working" data-hint="After is, use the activity form working." data-fix="Marcos is working from home today." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from home today.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Our live message says, “We are <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="waiting" data-hint="After are, use the activity form waiting." data-fix="We are waiting for the train." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> for the train.”</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: am, is, are + verb-ing</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Every present continuous verb phrase has two parts: a present form of <span class="ex">be</span> that agrees with the subject, and an <span class="ex">-ing</span> form that presents the activity as open.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>I</th><th>you / we / they</th><th>he / she / it</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>positive</b></td><td>I’m working.</td><td>We’re working.</td><td>She’s working.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>negative</b></td><td>I’m not working.</td><td>We aren’t working.</td><td>She isn’t working.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>question</b></td><td>Am I talking too fast?</td><td>Are you working?</td><td>Is she working?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Short answers use only the be verb: <span class="ex">Yes, I am. / Yes, she is. / No, they aren’t.</span> Never repeat the <span class="ex">-ing</span> verb, and do not contract a positive short answer.</p>

  <h2>Get to the root: an action viewed from inside</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The present continuous does more than say “now.” It presents an action as <strong>open and in progress</strong>. Imagine a video with a beginning and an end. The speaker places the camera somewhere between those two points. At that camera moment, the action is not finished.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>The mental picture</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">She is writing a report.</span></p>
    <p>The sentence does not tell us when she started or when she will finish. It tells us that the activity is open around the time we are talking about. She may pause for coffee and still be “writing a report” as her current project.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Has the report-writing started? <strong>Yes.</strong></li>
      <li>Is it presented as finished? <strong>No.</strong></li>
      <li>Must her pen be moving at this exact second? <strong>Not always.</strong> It can be a temporary activity around now.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h3>Why there are two verbs</h3>
  <p>English builds this meaning in two parts. The verb <span class="ex">be</span> carries the subject and tense: <span class="ex">I am</span>, <span class="ex">she is</span>, <span class="ex">they are</span>. The <span class="ex">-ing</span> verb names the unfolding activity. That is why <span class="ex">She working</span> is incomplete: the sentence has an activity, but no finite verb to anchor it.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>part</th><th>job</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>am / is / are</b></td><td>agrees with the subject; makes negatives and questions</td><td><span class="ex">Is</span> she working? She <span class="ex">isn’t</span> working.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>verb-ing</b></td><td>shows the activity as unfolding</td><td>She is <span class="ex">working</span>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Follow the moving part</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">She is working. → Is she working? → She isn’t working.</span></p>
    <p>Only <span class="ex">is</span> moves to the front or becomes negative. The <span class="ex">-ing</span> verb never changes. This is why <span class="ex">Do you are working?</span> mixes two different systems and is not the target form.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Spelling the -ing form</h3>
  <p>We add <span class="ex">-ing</span> to the base verb, but spelling sometimes protects the original sound. Most verbs simply add <span class="ex">-ing</span>; learn the high-value changes below as spelling patterns, not as a reason to guess every unfamiliar form.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>base verb</th><th>rule</th><th>-ing form</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>work, wait</td><td>just add <b>-ing</b></td><td><span class="ex">work → working</span>, <span class="ex">wait → waiting</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>make, write</td><td>drop the silent <b>e</b></td><td><span class="ex">make → making</span>, <span class="ex">write → writing</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>run, sit, begin</td><td>after one vowel plus one final consonant, double that consonant in a one-syllable verb or a verb stressed at the end</td><td><span class="ex">run → running</span>, <span class="ex">sit → sitting</span>, <span class="ex">begin → beginning</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>visit, open, snow, fix</td><td>do not double when the final syllable is unstressed or the word ends in <b>w</b> or <b>x</b></td><td><span class="ex">visiting · opening · snowing · fixing</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>study, stay</td><td>keep the <b>y</b></td><td><span class="ex">study → studying</span>, <span class="ex">stay → staying</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>lie, die</td><td>change <b>ie</b> to <b>y</b></td><td><span class="ex">lie → lying</span>, <span class="ex">die → dying</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Two common forms do not follow the silent-<span class="ex">e</span> row: <span class="ex">be → being</span> and <span class="ex">see → seeing</span>. When unsure, check the whole form rather than adding letters mechanically.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: contractions carry the spoken rhythm</h3>
    <p>In a neutral positive sentence, speakers usually join the subject and <span class="ex">be</span>: <span class="ex">I’m working, you’re waiting, she’s talking, we’re leaving</span>. The activity word normally receives the strongest beat: <span class="ex">I’m <strong>WORK</strong>ing</span>, not four equally strong words.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>written form</th><th>usual spoken chunk</th><th>main beat</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>I am working.</td><td>I’m working.</td><td><b>work</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>She is calling.</td><td>She’s calling.</td><td><b>call</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>They are waiting.</td><td>They’re waiting.</td><td><b>wait</b></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The ending <span class="ex">-ing</span> finishes with one nasal <em>ng</em> sound; do not release a separate hard <em>g</em>. In questions, link the small words smoothly and keep the activity clear: <span class="ex">Are-you <strong>WORK</strong>ing?</span> and <span class="ex">What-are-you <strong>DO</strong>ing?</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>A nearby future with an arrangement</h3>
    <p>The same open-situation viewpoint can describe a future arrangement when the context gives a future time and shows that people have organized it: <span class="ex">We're meeting the client at 10 tomorrow</span>. This is more than a general hope; the meeting is on the calendar.</p>
    <p>Keep the time context visible. <span class="ex">We're working</span> normally points to now or around now. <span class="ex">We're working this Friday</span> points to an arranged future shift. A later future lesson compares this use with plans, predictions, and schedules.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Each chunk matches its subject, positive or negative meaning, and stated present, temporary, or arranged-future context.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the natural chunk</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the subject first, then the context: is the sentence positive or negative? Choose the chunk people really say.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="’m working">’m working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="’s working">’s working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are working">are working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="isn’t working">isn’t working</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="aren’t working">aren’t working</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The fictional update says, “I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="’m working" data-hint="I takes am; in a positive spoken chunk, contract I am to I'm." data-fix="I'm working from home this week, so call me on my cell." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from home this week, so call me on my cell.”</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The profile states that Maya uses <span class="ex">she</span>. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="’s working" data-hint="She takes is; in a positive spoken chunk, contract she is to she's." data-fix="She's working in Chicago this month." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> in Chicago this month.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The live building notice says the builders <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are working" data-hint="The plural subject the builders takes are, and the sentence is positive." data-fix="The builders are working on the roof right now." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the roof right now, so it’s noisy.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The maintenance notice says the elevator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="isn’t working" data-hint="The singular subject the elevator takes is; the stairs instruction shows a negative meaning." data-fix="The elevator isn't working today, so take the stairs." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> today, so take the stairs.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The calendar states that we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="aren’t working" data-hint="We takes are; the office closure makes this arranged Friday shift negative." data-fix="We aren't working this Friday because the office is closed." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> this Friday. The office is closed for the holiday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Dan's confirmed schedule says he <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="’s working" data-hint="Dan is singular, and the confirmed schedule states a positive arrangement." data-fix="Dan's working late tonight." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> late tonight, so his household is planning dinner without him.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The project board assigns the same report to you and Priya. You and Priya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are working" data-hint="You and Priya is a plural subject, so use are working." data-fix="You and Priya are working on the same report." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the same report, so please share your notes.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The call diagnostics show no audio. My headphones <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="aren’t working" data-hint="Headphones has a plural form and the diagnostics show a negative result." data-fix="My headphones aren't working, so I can't hear the call." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> again, so I can’t hear the call.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Present simple or present continuous?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The difference is usually not the action itself. It is the <strong>speaker’s viewpoint</strong>. The present simple looks at a stable pattern from the outside; the present continuous looks at an open situation from the inside.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>present simple: routine or fact</th><th>present continuous: now, temporary, around now</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">I work at home.</span><br>That is my normal arrangement.</td><td><span class="ex">I’m working at home today.</span><br>This is the temporary situation now.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">She takes the bus.</span><br>That is her routine.</td><td><span class="ex">She’s taking a taxi.</span><br>That is happening on this occasion.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">What do you do?</span><br>What is your job or routine?</td><td><span class="ex">What are you doing?</span><br>What activity is in progress?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Time expressions are clues, not automatic rules. <span class="ex">Every day, usually</span> often support the present simple; <span class="ex">now, today, at the moment</span> often support the continuous. First understand the meaning, then use the clue.</p>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>State or action? Meaning comes first</h3>
    <p>Some verbs normally describe a state rather than an unfolding action: <span class="ex">know, understand, want, need, like</span>. At this level, use <span class="ex">I understand</span> and <span class="ex">I need help</span>, not <span class="ex">I’m understanding</span> or <span class="ex">I’m needing help</span>.</p>
    <p>A verb can change patterns when its meaning changes:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>state meaning</th><th>open activity meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="ex">I have a car.</span><br />Have means possession.</td><td><span class="ex">I'm having lunch.</span><br />Have is part of an activity.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="ex">I think the plan is good.</span><br />Think gives an opinion.</td><td><span class="ex">I'm thinking about the plan.</span><br />Think names an active process.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="ex">The menu looks good.</span><br />Look describes appearance.</td><td><span class="ex">I'm looking at the menu.</span><br />Look names an intentional action.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Do not choose only from the verb. Choose from the meaning the speaker needs.</p>
  </div>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read present-simple and present-continuous listening check">
    <h2>Listen: routine, state, or open situation?</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Your teacher reads each complete fictional context once at a natural speed and once more slowly. Listen before you choose.</p>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished a routine from a temporary situation, possession from an activity, a live question, and a future arrangement.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening check</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Listening choices">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="works">works</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is working">is working</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has">has</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is having">is having</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Are">Are</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Do">Do</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are meeting">are meeting</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="meet">meet</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The schedule is the same every weekday. Luis <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="works" data-hint="Listen for every weekday, which marks the stated routine." data-fix="Luis works at the clinic every weekday." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button> at the clinic every weekday.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Luis normally works at the clinic, but today he <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is working" data-hint="Listen for but today, which changes the normal arrangement temporarily." data-fix="Today Luis is working from home." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button> from home.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The profile says Maya owns one car. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has" data-hint="Here have means possession, a state." data-fix="Maya has one car." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button> one car.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The café photo shows Maya eating lunch now. She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is having" data-hint="Here have is part of the open activity have lunch." data-fix="Maya is having lunch now." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button> lunch now.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The caller wants to know about this moment: “<button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Are" data-hint="A present-continuous question begins with Are before you." data-fix="Are you waiting outside?" data-placeholder="listen">listen</button> you waiting outside?”</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The appointment is confirmed for tomorrow at 10. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are meeting" data-hint="A confirmed future appointment supports the arranged-future continuous form." data-fix="We are meeting the client at 10 tomorrow." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button> the client at 10 tomorrow.</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>Teacher: open the script after the learner checks</summary>
      <ol><li>The schedule is the same every weekday. Luis works at the clinic every weekday.</li><li>Luis normally works at the clinic, but today he is working from home.</li><li>The profile says Maya owns one car. She has one car.</li><li>The café photo shows Maya eating lunch now. She is having lunch now.</li><li>The caller wants to know about this moment: “Are you waiting outside?”</li><li>The appointment is confirmed for tomorrow at 10. We are meeting the client at 10 tomorrow.</li></ol>
    </details>
  </section>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill data-success-message="Correct. Each question moves the matching form of be before the subject, and each short answer keeps only that form of be.">
    <h3>Drill 2: type the question word or short answer</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Questions start with <b>Am</b>, <b>Is</b>, or <b>Are</b>. Short answers use the be verb alone, never the <b>-ing</b> verb.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Are" data-hint="The subject you takes are; move it to the front and capitalize it." data-fix="Are you working right now?" aria-label="Question starter before you working right now" /> you working right now?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Yes, I <input class="answer-input" data-answer="am" data-hint="The positive short answer to Are you...? is Yes, I am." data-fix="Yes, I am." aria-label="Positive short answer after Yes I" />.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The travel update states that Lena uses <span class="ex">she</span>. <input class="answer-input" data-answer="Is" data-hint="The subject Lena takes is; move it to the front and capitalize it." data-fix="Is Lena driving to the airport?" aria-label="Question starter before Lena driving to the airport" /> Lena driving to the airport?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>No, she <input class="answer-input" data-answer="isn’t" data-hint="The negative short answer to Is she...? keeps is and adds not." data-fix="No, she isn't." aria-label="Negative short answer after No she" />.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Am" data-hint="The subject I takes am; move it to the front and capitalize it." data-fix="Am I speaking too fast?" aria-label="Question starter before I speaking too fast" /> I speaking too fast?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>No, you <input class="answer-input" data-answer="aren’t" data-hint="The negative short answer to Am I...? uses you are not from the listener's viewpoint." data-fix="No, you aren't." aria-label="Negative short answer after No you" />.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A message from a coworker</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Where are you? We’re waiting outside the restaurant. Dana is parking the car, and Tom is holding a table for us inside. I’m looking at the menu now, and everything looks great. Are you still finishing that report?"</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You located the group's waiting place, Dana's current activity, and the report question addressed to the message recipient.">
    <h3>Drill 3: read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="outside the restaurant" data-hint="The second sentence states the group's location directly after waiting." data-fix="The group is waiting outside the restaurant.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Where is the group waiting?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="outside the restaurant">outside the restaurant</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="inside the office">inside the office</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at the station">at the station</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="parking the car" data-hint="The third sentence names Dana and her unfinished activity." data-fix="Dana is parking the car.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What is Dana doing right now?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="parking the car">parking the car</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="holding a table">holding a table</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="reading the menu">reading the menu</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the person reading the message" data-hint="The final question uses you and asks whether the recipient is still finishing a report." data-fix="The person receiving the message is probably still working on the report.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Who is probably still working?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the person reading the message">the person reading the message</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Tom">Tom</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Dana">Dana</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="is she taking the train" data-hint="Move Is before the subject she, then keep taking the train together." data-fix="Is she taking the train?" data-success-message="Correct. The question moves is before she and leaves the activity phrase taking the train unchanged.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">A live travel update is unclear. Build the question asking about her current trip.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="taking">taking</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">Is</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="train">train</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">she</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="we aren’t watching the game tonight" data-hint="Begin with We aren't, then keep watching the game together and place tonight last." data-fix="We aren't watching the game tonight." data-success-message="Correct. Aren't carries the negative after we, while watching stays in the verb-ing form.">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the negative</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The group has confirmed a different plan for tonight. Build the negative arrangement.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="watching">watching</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="we">We</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="game">game</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="aren’t">aren’t</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="tonight">tonight</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="working" data-hint="The sentence has an -ing activity but no subject-matched form of be." data-fix="She is working at the hospital now." data-why="The -ing verb cannot stand alone. Add is: she is working.">
    <h3>Drill 6: two verbs, not one</h3>
    <p>One small verb is missing. Tap the word that cannot stand alone.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">She</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="working">working</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hospital">at the hospital</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="now">now.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="do" data-hint="The phrase are working already contains the present-continuous helper needed for the question." data-fix="Are you working today?" data-why="Present continuous questions move are in front of the subject. Do belongs to the present simple system.">
    <h3>Drill 7: one system at a time</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="do">Do</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are working">are working</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="today">today?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: say it, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the cue, say the full sentence aloud, then reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I’m taking notes. Change to he.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He’s taking notes.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> They’re watching the game. Make it negative.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They aren’t watching the game.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> She’s cooking dinner. Ask the question.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Is she cooking dinner?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Are you listening? Answer yes.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Yes, I am.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> He drives to work. Make it about right now.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He’s driving to work right now.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> We’re waiting for the bus. Change to she.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She’s waiting for the bus.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to show your camera, room, street, screen, location, schedule, family, friends, or messages. Use a fictional scene card, a public image with a written description, or invented information. If a visual is not accessible, the teacher reads the scene card aloud.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Live scene card:</b> Invent or use a labeled public scene. Give five supported descriptions: <span class="ex">A bus is stopping. Two people are waiting. It isn't raining.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Routine versus today:</b> Create a fictional worker's normal schedule and one different day. Contrast three pairs: <span class="ex">Maya usually takes the bus, but today she's walking.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Information gap:</b> You and your teacher each receive a fictional live-update card. Ask focused questions such as <span class="ex">Is Luis working from home?</span> and <span class="ex">What is Maya doing?</span> Use short answers before adding details.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>State or action:</b> Explain the meaning difference in <span class="ex">He has lunch at noon</span>, <span class="ex">He is having lunch now</span>, and <span class="ex">He has a lunch reservation</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Arranged future:</b> Build a fictional calendar with three confirmed appointments. State the time or day clearly: <span class="ex">We're meeting the designer at 2 tomorrow.</span></div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: a two-time update</h3>
    <p>Give a 45- to 60-second fictional team update with a normal routine, the temporary situation now, and one confirmed future arrangement.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Use one accurate present-simple routine.</li>
      <li>Use two complete present-continuous statements with the correct form of <span class="ex">be</span>.</li>
      <li>Include one negative and one correctly ordered question.</li>
      <li>Use a state verb accurately or explain one state/action contrast.</li>
      <li>Give a clear future time with the arranged-future example.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The teacher asks one follow-up question. Repair one sentence if the context or time frame is unclear.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “The present continuous verb phrase needs two parts: a present form of ______ and an ______ form. For a question, the form of ______ moves in front of the subject. The core meaning is an open situation viewed from ______.”</p>
    <p>Then contrast a routine with a temporary situation, explain <span class="ex">I have lunch at noon</span> versus <span class="ex">I'm having lunch now</span>, and give one arranged future with a clear future time.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You selected complete forms from explicit time contexts, built questions and short answers, separated routines from temporary situations, and formed writing accurately.">
    <h3>Final quiz: forms and meaning</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is raining" data-hint="The live weather feed presents rain as in progress now; include the form of be and the -ing form." data-fix="The live weather feed says it is raining now.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. The live weather feed shows rain in progress now. It ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is raining">is raining</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="rains">rains</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="raining">raining</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Are you coming to the meeting now?" data-hint="To ask about the movement in progress, place Are before you and keep coming unchanged." data-fix="Are you coming to the meeting now?">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Your teammate says, “I'm walking toward the meeting now.” Ask about that movement in progress.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Are you coming to the meeting now?">Are you coming to the meeting now?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do you come to the meeting every week?">Do you come to the meeting every week?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Are you at the meeting already?">Are you at the meeting already?</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="aren’t" data-hint="The subject we takes are; add not to make the present-continuous statement negative." data-fix="We aren't watching the game; the office screen is off.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. The office screen is off, and nobody is streaming the game. We ___ watching it.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="aren’t">aren’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="don’t">don’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="isn’t">isn’t</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="isn’t" data-hint="The prompt requires a one-word negative short answer, so keep is and contract not." data-fix="Is Marta working today? No, she isn't.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. Complete the negative short answer with one word: “Is Marta working today?” “No, she ___.”</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="isn’t">isn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="not">not</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="doesn’t">doesn’t</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She’s taking the bus." data-hint="The live tracker presents the trip as in progress now." data-fix="The live tracker says she's taking the bus.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. A live tracker shows that her bus trip is in progress now. Which report fits?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She’s taking the bus.">She’s taking the bus.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She takes the bus.">She takes the bus.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She’s got a bus pass.">She’s got a bus pass.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="drink" data-hint="Every morning marks a routine, so use the present simple with I." data-fix="I drink coffee every morning.">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. I ___ coffee every morning.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="drink">drink</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="am drinking">am drinking</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="drinking">drinking</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a temporary situation" data-hint="This week limits the home-working arrangement to an open period around now." data-fix="I'm working from home this week describes a temporary situation.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. “I’m working from home this week” describes ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a temporary situation">a temporary situation</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a permanent fact">a permanent fact</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a finished action">a finished action</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="writing" data-hint="Write ends in a silent e, so drop that e before adding -ing." data-fix="The email is open and unfinished; she is writing it now.">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. The email is open on her screen and unfinished. She is ___ it now.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="writing">writing</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="written">written</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="writes">writes</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Return tomorrow before rereading the lesson. Complete the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute next-day retrieval</a>, then revisit only the form, time meaning, state/action contrast, or spelling pattern that still feels slow.</p>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day present-continuous retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a temporary continuous form, a simple routine, possession with has, and the activity is having lunch.">
      <h3>Choose from meaning, not from the verb alone</h3>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Next-day tense and meaning choices">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is working">is working</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="works">works</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has">has</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is having">is having</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Normally Maya works downtown, but today she <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is working" data-hint="But today marks a temporary change from the stated routine." data-fix="Today Maya is working from home." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> from home.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Her regular calendar says she <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="works" data-hint="Every Monday marks a regular routine." data-fix="She works downtown every Monday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> downtown every Monday.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The profile says Luis owns one car. He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has" data-hint="Here have means possession, so use the present simple form has." data-fix="Luis has one car." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> one car.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The café photo shows Luis eating now. He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is having" data-hint="Here have is part of the open activity have lunch." data-fix="Luis is having lunch now." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> lunch now.</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="working" data-hint="The sentence has an -ing form but no present form of be." data-fix="She is working today." data-why="The present continuous requires is before working with she.">
      <h3>Repair the missing form of be</h3>
      <p>Tap the activity form that cannot stand alone here.</p>
      <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">She</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="working">working</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="today">today.</button></div>
      <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
      <h3>Thirty-second retrieval</h3>
      <p>Without looking back, change <span class="ex">He works at home every day</span> to a temporary situation today. Then give one confirmed arrangement for tomorrow.</p>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
      <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He's working at home today.</strong> Example arrangement: <strong>He's meeting the team at 9 tomorrow.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>
